camchrome: WebGL readback coherence and getParameter timing.

Three measured tells in the farbling/override layer:

* readPixels may be handed a destination larger than the framebuffer; the noise
  pass rewrote bytes the spec says stay untouched. The perturb routine now takes
  a destination clip and the WebGL exit computes the in-bounds rectangle.
* readPixels into a PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER skipped the perturbation entirely, so the
  same framebuffer disagreed with the array exit. It now reads into a renderer
  copy, applies the identical clipped perturbation and uploads it.
* The persona answers UNMASKED_RENDERER, RED_BITS, DEPTH_BITS, SAMPLES and
  ALIASED_LINE_WIDTH_RANGE from memory, while Chrome pays a synchronous GPU
  round trip (~100 us) for each. A page can time the difference. Those calls now
  pay the same latency; values that Chrome caches (MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE) are not
  slowed.

